   repo-root-relative = <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F999-absent.md

a dispute cites an argument a human will read, so the entry must exist first.
write it there, then re-run this command:
  <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md

and pass either the ROUTE-relative path (canonical), or the repo-root-relative one:
  --why .fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md
  --why <tempDir>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F00N-<slug>.md"
`;

exports[`setStoneAsConcernAbsorbed.integration given: [case4] a dispute whose fulcrum must carry it when: [t0] the fulcrum has no frontmatter then: the dispute is refused, and the fix names every field 1`] = `
"✋ ConstraintError: the fulcrum this dispute cites has no frontmatter
   ├─ file: <route>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F010-bare.md
   ├─ absent
   │  ├─ case
   │  ├─ rework
   │  ├─ ground
   │  ├─ confidence
   │  ├─ status
   │  ├─ owed
   │  ├─ holds
   │  ├─ lean
   │  └─ verdict
   └─ fix: the frontmatter opens the file, with every field of
      ├─ case · rework · ground · confidence · status · owed · holds · lean · verdict
      └─ paste, at the head of the file
         ├─
         │  ---
         │  case: F010
         │  rework: clean            # clean | dirty
         │  ground: wrong            # wrong | dirty
         │  confidence: 0.65         # the weakest call it holds, 0 to 1
         │  status: open             # open | held | ruled | superseded
         │  owed: human              # derived: reflect iff ground wrong and confidence ≥ 0.90, else human
         │  holds: [limited/i001/blocker.1]
         │  lean: <one line — the call you made>
         │  verdict: null            # only rhx route.fulcrum.rule writes this
         │  ---
         └─

{
  "path": "<route>/.fulcrums/inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F010-bare.md",
  "reflect": null
}"
`;

